# Never skip UI build on UI change

## The rule

> **When any change in the change set touches `pim-offline-server/ui/**`
> (or other assets that feed the embedded admin SPA), deploy/build MUST
> run `Deploy-OfflineServerDev.ps1` without `-SkipUiBuild`, and MUST NOT
> pass `--features skip-ui-build` for that deploy. `-SkipUiBuild` /
> `skip-ui-build` is allowed only for pure Rust/backend changes with
> zero UI file changes in that same change set.**

## Why

The offline server binary embeds the Vite-built SPA (`ui-dist` / `ui/dist`)
at compile time. `-SkipUiBuild` (and Cargo `--features skip-ui-build`)
rebuilds or restages the Rust binary while leaving the previous embedded
bundle in place. Operators then hit a stale SPA — e.g. Current State
Compliance looked “never built” / wrong sidebar labels even though the
source and docs had already shipped.

## Required agent behavior

1. **UI touched this change set** (`pim-offline-server/ui/**`, embedded
   UI asset paths, or any edit that must appear in the admin browser):
   - Run
     `pwsh c:\analog-pim\pim-offline-server\scripts\Deploy-OfflineServerDev.ps1`
     with **no** `-SkipUiBuild`.
   - Do **not** pass `--features skip-ui-build` on the deploy’s
     `cargo build` / equivalent.
2. **Pure Rust / backend only** (no UI paths in the same change set):
   `-SkipUiBuild` / `skip-ui-build` remains allowed to avoid a needless
   npm/Vite cycle.
3. **Do not claim UI is live** after a SkipUi deploy. If you skipped the
   UI build, say so; do not treat the running service as proof of the
   new SPA.

## Forbidden

- `Deploy-OfflineServerDev.ps1 -SkipUiBuild` when `ui/**` (or embedded
  UI assets) changed in the same work.
- `cargo build --features skip-ui-build` (or equivalent) as the deploy
  build for a UI change set.
- Assuming “service RUNNING” means the new React pages are served.

